  "description_html": "Size comparison between a juvenile <i>Tarbosaurus</i> at age of about 3 years.<sup id=\"cite_ref-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup> (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://scienceblogs.com/laelaps/2008/07/a_new_juvenile_tarbosaurus.php\">based on a specimen found in Mongolia, the summer of 2006</a>), and the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Fossil\" title=\"Fossil\">fossil</a> of the <a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tyrannosauridae\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tyrannosauridae\">Tyrannosaurid</a> specimen <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://web.archive.org/web/20070110004506/www.paleograveyard.com/shanshanosaurus.html\">IVPP V4878</a>, described as <i>Shanshanosaurus huoyansaniensis</i> (Dong, 1977). IVPP V4878 has in the years after it was described as <i>Shanshanosaurus huoyansaniensis</i> is regarded as a juvenile <i>Tarbosaurus</i>. IVPP V4878 and the 3-year old <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Tarbosaurus\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tarbosaurus\">Tarbosaurus</a></i> are of similar size. Their <i><a href=\"//commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?title=Maxilla&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Maxilla (page does not exist)\">maxilla</a></i> are also very similar in shape, as well as size. The juvenile <i>Tarbosaurus</i> have a skull about 28 cm. long<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://cache.daylife.com/imageserve/09oLaoQ0zbbhU/610x.jpg\">[1]</a>, and the lower jaw of IVPP V4878 measure about 25-26 cm (<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"http://i16.photobucket.com/albums/b1/Qilongia/RaptorexShanshanTarbo.jpg\">[2]</a>, IVPP V4878 is C. in the image.\n<div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"References\">References</h4></div>\n<ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-1\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\">Tsuihiji T <i>et.al.</i> (2011), <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.oucom.ohiou.edu/dbms-witmer/Downloads/2011_Tsuihiji_et_al._Tarbosaurus_juvenile_skull.pdf\">\"Cranial Osteology of a Juvenile Specimen of <i>Tarbosaurus bataar</i> (Theropoda, Tyrannosauridae) from the Nemegt Formation (Upper Cretaceous) of Bugin Tsav, Mongolia\"</a>, <i>Journal of Vertebrate Paleontology</i> <b>31</b>(3): p. 497-517.</span>\n</li>\n</ol>",
